Attacks attempted (all in a /tmp scratch copy except where noted; worktree itself
never mutated):

1. INVARIANT FUZZING (attack surface 1). Wrote a standalone Go test file
   (adversarial_test.go, deleted after use) exercising: leap-year Feb,
   single-day range, mid-month start/end, empty-middle-month, >6-month
   range (cap+carry-in), zero combined target (series must be nil),
   income-only month, healthcare-only month, and a 500-iteration random
   fuzz over ranges up to ~400 days with random transaction dates/types/
   amounts and random targets. All asserted |tail - (-CombinedCumulativeDelta)|
   <= 0.01. Result: 100% pass, including the 500-case fuzz
   (`go test ./internal/services/metrics/ -run TestAdversarial -v`).
   Also tested a 25-year range (300 synthetic monthly transactions) to
   probe float-accumulation drift: actual diff was 6e-10, nowhere near the
   $0.01 tolerance the tests use — the tolerance is generous headroom, not
   a sign the implementation is actually noisy. (First attempt at this
   25-year case produced a 3631-diff "failure" — traced to my own test bug:
   I passed an unfiltered TransactionSet with transactions dated past
   rangeEnd, violating the documented pre-filtered-TransactionSet
   precondition. Fixed by filtering with FilterByDateRange first, which
   made the diff vanish to noise level. This confirms the precondition is
   load-bearing and is correctly documented as such in dashboard.go.)

2. MUTATION TESTING against the ACTUAL project test suite (not my own),
   in the scratch copy:
   a. Reintroduced the pre-fix bug shape — capped to last 6 points by
      re-summing from zero instead of preserving carry-in. Result:
      `TestCalculateMetrics_CombinedCumulativeBalance_MoreThanSixMonths_CapsAndCarriesIn`
      correctly FAILed (tail 3045.17 vs want 3983.57). Every other new/
      tightened test still passed (as expected, since only the >6-month
      case exercises the cap).
   b. Replaced fractional accrual (`combinedTarget * MonthsBetween(...)`)
      with flat integer-month accrual (`combinedTarget`). Result: 5 of 6
      CombinedCumulativeBalance tests correctly FAILed (Accumulates...,
      LastIsNegationOf..., MoreThanSixMonths..., PartialMonthRange...,
      ZeroTransactionMiddleMonth...), each with a clear diff far outside
      $0.01. Confirms the tightened $0.01 tests genuinely catch
      month-rounding regressions, not just gross breakage.
   Both mutations restored before discarding the scratch copy; the real
   worktree was never touched.

3. CROSS-VERSION TREND IDENTITY (criterion 7, "byte-identical"). Rather
   than eyeballing the diff, added an identical throwaway test to both
   this worktree and a `git worktree add --detach origin/master` checkout,
   generating 200 randomized (range, transaction-set, targets) fixtures
   and dumping IncomeTrend/ExpensesTrend/SavingsTrend/HealthcareTrend/
   LivingExpensesTrend/TrendLabels/CumulativeDelta/HealthcareCumulativeDelta/
   CombinedCumulativeDelta to JSON from each. `diff` of the two JSON
   files was empty across all 200 cases — the non-balance trend arrays and
   the delta fields are provably unchanged, not just "looks unchanged in
   the diff." Scratch worktree removed afterward.

4. JS/TEMPLATE SEAM (attack surface 3). Manually traced initSparklines
   (charts.js ~563-590) and renderSparkline's balance branch (~283-291):
   nb defaults to 0 when data-neutral-band is absent/non-finite/<=0, and
   `v > 0`/`v < 0` (nb=0) is byte-identical to the pre-diff `v>0`/`v<0`
   fill logic — confirmed by reading both the pre-diff and post-diff
   branches side by side (`git show origin/master:web/static/js/charts.js`
   vs current). Grepped the whole template tree for `data-mode="balance"`
   and `sparkline-`: `#sparkline-budget` is the ONLY balance-mode
   sparkline on the site; income/expenses/monthly/healthcare sparklines
   have no `data-mode` attribute and are unaffected. `{{.BudgetVerdict.Eps}}`
   is a Go float64 constant (1.0) rendered via html/template's default
   Sprint formatting ("1"), always present (Eps is set unconditionally on
   every BuildBudgetVerdict return path, including the nil-metrics and
   no-target early returns — verified in verdict.go and covered by two
   `Eps != 1.0` assertions in verdict_test.go). No numeric eps literal
   appears in kpis.html (grepped the diff).

5. DEAD-BAND KNIFE EDGE (attack surface 4). Card classifies on raw
   CombinedCumulativeDelta vs exactly onBudgetEps=1.0; chart classifies on
   tail vs neutralBand=1.0 where tail equals -delta only up to float noise
   (empirically ~1e-9 to 1e-6, per fuzzing above, not $0.01 in practice).
   A disagreement is only theoretically possible in a sub-cent window
   around the exact eps boundary, which is below any dollar amount either
   UI element displays (formatMoney rounds to cents) and is explicitly
   covered by the spec's own "up to float noise" framing and the tests'
   $0.01 tolerance. Not a practical defect.

6. SCOPE (attack surface 6). `git diff --name-only origin/master` lists
   exactly the manifest's 7 files plus `.swarm/ledger.tsv` (lead-owned,
   excluded per instructions). No out-of-territory files touched.

7. FULL GATES in the actual worktree (not the scratch copy):
