8. Independently reviewed checker-a11y's Y1.1 verdict (PASS) against the
   actual kpis.html/charts.js diff and agree with its reasoning: only a
   data-* attribute added (not exposed to the a11y tree, no aria-*
   reference), fill colors byte-identical, the diff can only remove a fill
   segment from a data point (never add/recolor), so no new 1.4.1 or
   contrast regression. Pre-existing missing text-alternative for Plotly
   sparklines (ACCESSIBILITY point 11) is untouched by this diff and
   correctly flagged as backlog, not a Y1 defect.

No attack landed. Strongest surviving concern (not a FAIL): the tail/delta
agreement is proven only "within $0.01," not exactly bit-for-bit, so there
exists a theoretical sub-cent classification disagreement window at the
exact ±$1 boundary; empirically the actual noise is 4-6 orders of magnitude
smaller than that tolerance even at a 25-year range, so this is a
documented, accepted approximation rather than a live defect.

VERDICT: PASS
